From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raag Jadav <raag.jadav@intel.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:42:28 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] drm/xe: Move xe_device_wedged_fini() registration to
 xe_device_probe_early()

The device can be declared wedged while processing boot-time hardware
errors, which can result in PM reference leak if driver probe fails
before xe_device_wedged_fini() is registered.

Early register the required cleanup action and fix this.

Fixes: a7df563b45b0 ("drm/xe/xe_hw_error: Handle CSC Firmware reported Hardware errors")
Signed-off-by: Raag Jadav <raag.jadav@intel.com>
Reviewed-by: Rodrigo Vivi <rodrigo.vivi@intel.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261022051303.282805-5-raag.jadav@intel.com
Signed-off-by: Matt Roper <matthew.d.roper@intel.com>
(cherry-picked from commit 6599a0eb0990cde96c4e66a4e1e2ae1b172e85d2 linux-next)
Signed-off-by: SYS SEOS AUTOBACKPORT <sys_seos_autobackport@intel.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_device.c | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_device.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_device.c
index 83dad6d2a376..67055c3b0991 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_device.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_device.c
@@ -801,6 +801,8 @@ static int xe_device_vram_alloc(struct xe_device *xe)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static void xe_device_wedged_fini(struct drm_device *drm, void *arg);
+
 /**
  * xe_device_probe_early: Device early probe
  * @xe: xe device instance
@@ -870,6 +872,10 @@ int xe_device_probe_early(struct xe_device *xe)
 	if (err)
 		return err;
 
+	err = drmm_add_action_or_reset(&xe->drm, xe_device_wedged_fini, xe);
+	if (err)
+		return err;
+
 	return 0;
 }
 ALLOW_ERROR_INJECTION(xe_device_probe_early, ERRNO); /* See xe_pci_probe() */
@@ -1197,10 +1203,6 @@ int xe_device_probe(struct xe_device *xe)
 
 	detect_preproduction_hw(xe);
 
-	err = drmm_add_action_or_reset(&xe->drm, xe_device_wedged_fini, xe);
-	if (err)
-		goto err_unregister_display;
-
 	/*
 	 * Process and log any errors detected by hardware. Possible results can
 	 * include declaring the device as wedged, which must be done only after
-- 
2.43.0

